From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flysoft <flysoftbeta@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:39:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] prts: precise fake vsync timer in remote mode (headless has
 no DXGI output)

The cloaked headless window has no matching DXGI output, so the vsync thread
fell back to Sleep(17 ms) + re-enumeration (~53 fps). In remote mode with
--fake-vsync-rate, use a drift-free high-resolution timer. The GPU process
receives --prts-remote so the hook shares the remote-mode guard.

Patch-Name: 17-remote-vsync

diff --git a/content/browser/gpu/gpu_process_host.cc b/content/browser/gpu/gpu_process_host.cc
index 1b29f20028..6e2811abcf 100644
--- a/content/browser/gpu/gpu_process_host.cc
+++ b/content/browser/gpu/gpu_process_host.cc
@@ -1389,6 +1389,10 @@ bool GpuProcessHost::LaunchGpuProcess() {
   // https://crbug.com/590825
   // If you want a browser command-line switch passed to the GPU process
   // you need to add it to |kSwitchNames| at the beginning of this file.
+  // PRTS: The GPU vsync hook shares the process-wide remote-mode guard.
+  if (ui::IsPrtsRemoteMode()) {
+    cmd_line->AppendSwitch(switches::kPrtsRemote);
+  }
   cmd_line->CopySwitchesFrom(browser_command_line, kSwitchNames);
   cmd_line->CopySwitchesFrom(browser_command_line,
                              switches::kGLSwitchesCopiedFromGpuProcessHost);
